{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And I will remove his blood</b> — that he used to consume the blood of the slain; he will return to the service of HaShem." "<b>and his detestable things</b> — the impurity that he used to consume among the Philistines, or an allusion to idolatry." "<b>And he too will remain</b> — the sense is: none of the Philistines will remain except he who serves HaShem blessed be He publicly." "<b>like a chieftain in Judah</b> — like the choicest of Judah in the service of HaShem." "<b>and Ekron like the Jebusite</b> — he will give the tribute of the Jebusite, which was in Jerusalem in the days of David and after him, for they gave tribute to the kings of Judah."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:46:28.050700428Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}